<html>
<title>Navigation</title>
<body>


<h1>Navigation</h1>

<p>
This section describes the different navigation options on the <strong>Direct Assembler</strong> tab.
</p>

<p>
The navigation controls are shown below:
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/assembler_navigation.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Navigation</strong> scrollbar</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Move to:</strong> field</li>
</ul>

<p>
The scrollbar (1) can be used to move through the code. The top of the scrollbar corresponds to address 0 and the bottom to FFFF (hexadecimal).
The <tt>UP</tt> and <tt>DOWN</tt> arrow keys move the code one line at a time; <tt>SHIFT UP</tt> or <tt>SHIFT DOWN</tt> move the code one page at a time.
Alternatively, an address can be specified in the <strong>Move to:</strong> field (2), which will move the view directly to the specified address.
</p>

</body>
</html>
